course: dictionary
lesson: 343
title: Feelings words: annoyed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Annoyed means a bit angry or irritated about something. «I was annoyed when my brother took my pens.» The pens were yours, so you felt a little cross. Annoyed is milder than angry or furious.
explain: Annoyed can also be the verb form of annoy, which means to make someone a bit angry. «The noise annoyed the neighbours.» The noise did the annoying, and the neighbours were the ones who felt annoyed. Ask yourself who feels it and who causes it.
explain: You can be annoyed with someone, or annoyed about or at something. «Get annoyed» is another way to say it. When you feel annoyed, calm ways help: take a breath, say how you feel, or walk away for a moment.
explain: Writers use feelings words to show how a character is feeling. «Ears pinned flat back are a warning that a horse is angry or annoyed.» The word annoyed sits beside angry, so you can tell it is a strong feeling but not the strongest. Clues in the words around it help you check.
fact: Annoyed means a bit angry or irritated.
fact: Annoy is the verb. Its forms are annoys, annoyed and annoying.
fact: Annoyed is milder than angry or furious.
fact: «Round the bend» means mad or very annoyed.
fact: «Salty» means annoyed in some talk.
exercise: «I was annoyed when my brother took my pens.» What does annoyed mean here? | Tired after a long walk | * A bit angry or irritated | Very happy and excited | Lost and afraid
exercise: «The noise annoyed the neighbours.» Who or what made someone a bit angry? | The garden | The neighbours | The sunshine | * The noise
exercise: Which word means a bit angry? | Curt | * Annoyed | Barely | Famished
test: «Ears pinned flat back are a warning that a horse is angry or annoyed.» What does annoyed mean in this sentence? | * A bit angry or irritated | Quiet and gentle | Very old | Hungry
test: «You're driving me round the bend.» What does round the bend mean? | Happy and laughing | Walking in a circle | * Mad or very annoyed | Lost on a path
exam: Which is a calm way to deal with feeling annoyed? | Kick the chair | * Take a breath and say how you feel | Slam the door | Shout at the nearest person
